course: dictionary
lesson: 2070
title: Words that keep going
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Constant can mean happening all the time, or again and again. In Alice's story, from inside comes «a constant howling and sneezing», so the noise never stops. Read the words around it: howling and sneezing are things that keep going, so constant means never stopping.
explain: Constant can also mean staying the same, not changing. A car that drives at a constant speed keeps the same speed the whole time. Ask: would "the same" fit in this sentence? If it does, you have the right meaning.
explain: In maths and science, a constant is a noun: a number or amount that does not change. The number of days in a week is a constant. Mercator's map uses the idea too: «a straight line is a line of constant compass bearing», which means the direction stays the same all along the line.
explain: Old and literary books use constant to mean loyal and faithful, like a friend who always stands by you. This meaning is rare today, so check the sentence clues before you choose it.
fact: Constant means happening all the time or again and again, as in «a constant reminder».
fact: Constant means staying the same, not changing, as in «drive at a constant speed».
fact: In maths and science, a constant is a number or amount that does not change, like the number of days in a week.
fact: In science, things kept constant are controlled so that a test is fair.
fact: In old or literary writing, constant means loyal and faithful, as in «a constant friend».
exercise: «From inside comes a constant howling and sneezing.» What does constant mean here? | Loyal and faithful | A number that does not change | Staying the same, never changing | *Happening all the time
exercise: Maths problem: «The car travels at a constant speed.» What does this mean? | *The same speed all the way | Stopped for a rest | Going faster and faster | Shaking from side to side
exercise: In maths, what is a constant? | *A number or amount that does not change | A shape with four sides | A question with many answers | A word that means loyal
test: Mercator's map: «a straight line is a line of constant compass bearing». What does constant mean here? | Old and worn out | Changing all the time | *Staying the same | Very loud
test: «Constant pretending can feel tiring.» What does constant mean here? | A number in maths | Not changing at all | *Happening again and again | Faithful and loyal
exam: «He has been a constant friend to me.» What does constant mean here? | Changing often | Happening once only | *Loyal and faithful | A number that does not change
